      "title": "AOP Concepts and the Proxy Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "AOP Concepts and the Proxy Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Vocabulary",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Term",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Aspect==",
                  "`@Aspect` + `@Component` class holding logging, transactions or security, away from business code"
                ],
                [
                  "==Join point==",
                  "A **method execution** on a Spring bean (no field or constructor)"
                ],
                [
                  "==Pointcut==",
                  "Predicate that selects join points"
                ],
                [
                  "==Advice==",
                  "Code run at those join points"
                ],
                [
                  "==Advisor==",
                  "One pointcut paired with one advice"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Proxy Mental Model",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caller",
                    "sub": "gets the proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Proxy",
                    "sub": "runs advice",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Target",
                    "sub": "real bean",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==BeanPostProcessor== wraps the target in a proxy at startup",
                "Callers hold the **proxy**, never the target",
                "An aspect is a pointcut string plus an advice method"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Aspect @Component",
                "class Audit {",
                "  @Before(\"execution(* com.app.service.*.*(..))\")",
                "  void log() { }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Spring AOP vs AspectJ",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Spring AOP",
                "AspectJ"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Weaving",
                  "==Runtime== proxies",
                  "Bytecode, compile or load time"
                ],
                [
                  "Join points",
                  "Bean method executions",
                  "Field, constructor, **self-call**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No proxy, no advice",
              "text": "Spring AOP only advises calls that cross the ==proxy==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Advice Types and Pointcut Expressions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Advice Types and Pointcut Expressions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Five Advice Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Advice",
                "Runs",
                "Changes result?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`@Before`",
                  "before the method",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`@AfterReturning(returning=)`",
                  "on normal return",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`@AfterThrowing(throwing=)`",
                  "on exception",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`@After`",
                  "==always==, finally-style",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`@Around`",
                  "wraps the call",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@Around` takes ==ProceedingJoinPoint==; must call `proceed()` and **return** it",
                "It can skip, retry, change args or swallow exceptions",
                "Only type that ==controls execution==",
                "Pick the **weakest** type that works"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Around(\"@annotation(Timed)\")",
                "public Object time(ProceedingJoinPoint pjp) throws Throwable {",
                "  long t = System.nanoTime();",
                "  try { return pjp.proceed(); }",
                "  finally { log(System.nanoTime() - t); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "times every @Timed method"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Order and Pointcuts",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Around",
                    "sub": "before",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Before",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Method",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AfterReturning",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "After",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Around",
                    "sub": "after",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "On exception, {red:AfterThrowing} replaces AfterReturning",
                "Several aspects: `@Order`, ==lower value runs first== on the way in"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Designator",
                "Matches"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`execution(* com.app.service.*.*(..))`",
                  "method signature"
                ],
                [
                  "`within(com.app.service..*)`",
                  "package tree"
                ],
                [
                  "`@annotation(com.app.Audited)`",
                  "annotated methods"
                ],
                [
                  "`@within`",
                  "annotated classes"
                ],
                [
                  "`args()`",
                  "argument types"
                ],
                [
                  "`bean(orderService)`",
                  "bean by name"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`@Around` that forgets to ==return proceed()== gives the caller **null**",
                "Using `@Around` when `@Before` or `@After` is enough"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
