    {
      "title": "JDK Dynamic Proxy vs CGLIB",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "JDK Dynamic Proxy vs CGLIB",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Two Proxy Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "JDK proxy",
                "CGLIB"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Built by",
                  "`java.lang.reflect.Proxy` + `InvocationHandler`",
                  "runtime **subclass**, overrides methods"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs interface",
                  "{red:yes}, at least one",
                  "{green:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "Instance of concrete class",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which One Spring Picks",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Plain Spring: bean has interfaces → ==JDK==, else ==CGLIB==",
                "Spring Boot 2+: ==CGLIB== by default (`spring.aop.proxy-target-class=true`)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@EnableAspectJAutoProxy(proxyTargetClass = true)"
              ],
              "note": "force CGLIB in plain Spring"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "CGLIB limits",
              "items": [
                "`final` class: cannot be proxied",
                "`final` or `private` method: not intercepted",
                "Call runs on the proxy, whose fields are unset: state may be {red:null}"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Inject by concrete class under JDK proxy",
              "text": "Gives ==BeanNotOfRequiredTypeException==. Inject the **interface** or use CGLIB."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check with `bean.getClass()`: `$$SpringCGLIB` or `jdk.proxy` in the name"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Self-Invocation: Why @Transactional and @Cacheable Get Skipped",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Self-Invocation: Why @Transactional and @Cacheable Get Skipped",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Bypass",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Advice lives in the ==proxy==, not in the target",
                "`this.method()` goes straight to the target and **skips the proxy**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caller",
                    "sub": "holds proxy",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Proxy",
                    "sub": "advice runs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "outer()",
                    "sub": "on target",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this.inner()",
                    "sub": "no advice",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Transactional(propagation = REQUIRES_NEW)",
                "public void inner() { }",
                "public void outer() { this.inner(); }"
              ],
              "note": "outer() is proxied, but inner() gets no REQUIRES_NEW"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`inner()` runs with ==no new transaction==, no rollback rules",
                "Same cause skips `@Cacheable`, `@Async`, `@Retryable`, `@PreAuthorize`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fixes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fix",
                "How"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1 (preferred)",
                  "Move `inner()` to **another bean**, inject it"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "Inject self with `@Lazy` or `ApplicationContext`"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "`AopContext.currentProxy()` with `exposeProxy=true`"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "AspectJ `mode=ASPECTJ`: ==no proxy== at all"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Related Gotchas",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`private` or package-private methods are ignored: ==public== needed",
                "`new Foo()` is not a bean: **no proxy**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Only calls that ==cross the proxy== get advice. Same-bean calls never do."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How Proxies Power Transactions, Security and Caching",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "How Proxies Power Transactions, Security and Caching",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. @Transactional",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Begin",
                    "sub": "get connection",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "proceed()",
                    "sub": "run method",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "sub": "normal return",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rollback",
                    "sub": "RuntimeException / Error",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`TransactionInterceptor` is an ==@Around== advice",
                "Checked exceptions need `rollbackFor`",
                "State is bound to the **thread**: lost in new threads and `@Async`",
                "`REQUIRED` joins; `REQUIRES_NEW` suspends and starts new"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Security and Caching",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Annotation",
                "Interceptor does",
                "Needs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`@PreAuthorize`",
                  "checks before `proceed()`, else AccessDeniedException",
                  "`@EnableMethodSecurity`"
                ],
                [
                  "`@PostAuthorize`",
                  "checks returned value",
                  "same"
                ],
                [
                  "`@Cacheable`",
                  "hit skips method; miss stores",
                  "`@EnableCaching`"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CachePut`",
                  "always runs, updates",
                  "same"
                ],
                [
                  "`@CacheEvict`",
                  "removes entries",
                  "same"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Swallowed exception",
              "text": "Catch without rethrow: the proxy sees a normal return and ==commits==. Interceptor order matters: caching before commit keeps rolled-back data."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why no rollback on IOException?** Only RuntimeException/Error by default.",
                "**Why no transaction in @Async?** Transaction state is thread-bound.",
                "**@CachePut vs @Cacheable?** CachePut always runs the method."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
